  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given circles&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;and</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>18</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>78</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>Thus, centers of two circles are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and radii are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;respectively.</p><p>Since, center&nbsp;of circles are on the opposite side of line&nbsp;<math><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>27</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>31</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>31</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>i</mi></mfenced></math><br /><br />Since, circles should not intersect given line.</p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow><msqrt><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>1</mn><mtext>&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;</mtext><mo>&#38;</mo><mtext>&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;</mtext><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>31</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow><msqrt><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>5</mn><mtext>&#8201;&#8201;</mtext><mo>&#38;</mo><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>31</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>10</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>21</mn></math>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>41</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Thus,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>i</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8745;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8745;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>12,</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>21</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p>",
